{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If it be torn in pieces, let him bring it for a witness</b> — by the hand of a predatory beast. <b>He shall bring it for a witness</b> — he shall bring witnesses that it was torn under duress, and he is exempt. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Exodus 22:12).\n\nBut one may wonder: why does Scripture here require witnesses, when above it says, \"the oath of YHWH shall be between them both,\" and the law concerning them is identical — that if he has witnesses, he is exempt for an animal that died, was maimed, was captured, and likewise for one that was torn; and if he has no witnesses, he swears concerning all of them and does not pay.\n\nPerhaps it is because Scripture speaks of the typical case: when an ox dies in its owner's stall, or climbs up a crag and is maimed, there is no witness to it, and likewise the one captured by armed bandits who came upon it and took it from the flock and went his way — but the lion and the bear, when they tear prey, a full complement of shepherds is called out over it, and therefore Scripture says that he shall bring them before a court and be exempt.\n\nOr perhaps Scripture comes to teach the law of Isi ben Yehudah, who says (Bava Metzia 83a), \"If no man saw it\" (Exodus 22:9) — he is exempt; the inference is that if there was a witness, he shall bring witnesses and be exempt. And its meaning is that if the incident of duress occurred in a place where people are present there all day, they do not rely on his oath, and he must bring the witnesses. And the manner of a tearing is that it would be so, as we have said, and therefore Scripture required in this case that he bring the witnesses.\n\nAnd Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 22:12): \"He shall bring it for a witness\" — that he shall bring part of the torn carcass, two legs or a piece of an ear, to serve as his witness. And so I found in the Mekhilta of Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai: Abba Shaul says, \"He shall bring a remnant,\" as it is said (Amos 3:12), \"Thus says YHWH: As the shepherd rescues from the mouth of the lion two legs...\" etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:14:09.457975225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}